Marta S: thanks bot. I'll patch the anchor and fix the broken SDK link (turn into https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk-go README canonical link).

Noor A: Also, add a short note in the changelog entry for this release: "Docs: standardize array envelope (`envelope_type` + `entries`) and add SDK normalization snippets (Go, Ruby)." That helps users searching release notes.

Ben L: quick question  should SDKs auto-wrap the array on the client side too, or only server-side docs recommend?

Marta S: recommendation is server-side production output should use envelope. SDKs can optionally auto-wrap client-side returned raw arrays to help adopters, but we should call it out as a compatibility helper in SDK docs, not silently change user data shapes.

Carlos V: CI note: I ran the docs build locally; images and code blocks render fine after the anchor fix.

